<!--
    kuna issue testcase: a position-independent ARM function's GOT base or
    literal-pool word lost by the cross-reference index when it sits far from
    its use, across a branch, or in a stack slot
    (`option picpoolreach on|off`, default-ON).

    Issue:      kuna-analysis-picpoolreach - `kuna xrefs` to a GOT slot or a
                string answered nothing when the `ldr rB,[pc,#..]; add rB,pc,rB`
                pair, or the GOT offset load, was more than eight instructions
                from its use or across a branch, or when the base was spilled
                to the stack and reloaded.
    Stage:      P1 code/data partition - the on-demand cross-reference query
                (`listing/xrefs.rs`, `listing/kuna_picpool.rs`).
    P0 assert:  `option picpoolreach on|off`.

    The Listing tier and the xref query are built only on the real-object
    bootstrap path, never on the console decompile path (docs/spec/
    01-program-prep.md section 1.6), and no console command prints an xref
    row, so a stage test cannot assert the row itself. This case pins what
    the console can show, as `kuna-armpltslot.xml` does for its option:

      * `option picpoolreach off` parses and round-trips (an unknown option
        would make the console error and the next decompile would not run),
      * flipping it changes nothing in the rendered C of `arm_timers`, which
        reads its callbacks through GOT slots,
      * the catalog documents it as a default-on P1 option.

    The two-pass proof (option off = the eight-instruction, fall-through-only
    window and no stack slots, default = the far, branched and spilled values
    reach their use) lives in the cargo gate `decompiler/crates/kuna-cli/
    tests/arm_regvalue.rs` (`picpoolreach_off_files_none_of_them` and the
    default tests), over the authored `arm_regvalue_le32.py` image.

    The XML wrapper only supplies the harness architecture; the pass clears it
    and loads the real linked ARM fixture (built from
    decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/gotxref_arm_le32.c).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/gotxref_arm_le32</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load function arm_timers</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option picpoolreach off</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option picpoolreach on</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>phase catalog picpoolreach</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
